1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,700
Hello again!

2
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:05,580
Last time, in Beat the Beads, you remembered all eighteen formulas.

3
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:08,680
I promised you a brand new kind of trick.

4
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:12,020
One that adds and takes away, both at once.

5
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:14,100
Today, it is here.

6
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:16,760
It helps when the big friend gets stuck.

7
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:24,320
A reminder: the big friend takes the friend off the ones rod, then carries one bead to the tens rod.

8
00:00:24,940 --> 00:00:25,560
You tell me.

9
00:00:26,060 --> 00:00:27,540
What is six's big friend?

10
00:00:29,560 --> 00:00:30,200
Four!

11
00:00:30,960 --> 00:00:32,440
But here is a problem.

12
00:00:33,160 --> 00:00:35,940
Sometimes the ones rod cannot give the friend away.

13
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:40,200
There are not enough lower beads showing, and the upper bead is down.

14
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:42,880
Then the big friend alone gets stuck.

15
00:00:43,380 --> 00:00:44,460
We need something more.

16
00:00:45,640 --> 00:00:46,580
Good news.

17
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:48,360
The small friend can help.

18
00:00:48,360 --> 00:00:52,580
Four's small friend is one, and four and one make five.

19
00:00:53,060 --> 00:00:56,100
The big friend and the small friend, working together.

20
00:00:56,520 --> 00:00:58,200
That is called the family.

21
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:00,980
So, look at the ones rod first.

22
00:01:01,540 --> 00:01:04,600
If the big friend gets stuck like that, call the family.

23
00:01:05,480 --> 00:01:06,540
Let us see it.

24
00:01:07,160 --> 00:01:08,180
Seven plus six.

25
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:10,580
Make seven on the ones rod.

26
00:01:11,060 --> 00:01:13,320
Push two lower beads up with your thumb.

27
00:01:14,020 --> 00:01:17,020
Then push the upper bead down with your index finger.

28
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:21,440
Remember: up is the thumb, and down is the index finger.

29
00:01:21,440 --> 00:01:25,220
Six's friend is four, so take away four.

30
00:01:25,760 --> 00:01:27,700
How many lower beads can we take away?

31
00:01:29,660 --> 00:01:30,740
Only two!

32
00:01:31,320 --> 00:01:32,200
We need four.

33
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:35,120
The big friend is stuck, just like we said.

34
00:01:35,980 --> 00:01:39,240
Plus six equals minus four, plus ten.

35
00:01:39,740 --> 00:01:41,860
But the small friend can take away four.

36
00:01:41,860 --> 00:01:44,280
Add one, then take away five.

37
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:48,000
Minus four equals plus one, minus five.

38
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:49,420
Put them together.

39
00:01:49,940 --> 00:01:52,020
Here is the family trick for adding.

40
00:01:52,820 --> 00:01:56,900
Plus six equals plus one, minus five, plus ten.

41
00:01:57,960 --> 00:01:58,680
Why?

42
00:01:59,320 --> 00:02:02,780
Plus ten adds four too many, so we take four away.

43
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:04,640
Remember our rule.

44
00:02:05,220 --> 00:02:08,360
Ones rod first, and lower beads before the upper bead.

45
00:02:08,920 --> 00:02:09,680
Plus one.

46
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:11,560
Push one lower bead up.

47
00:02:12,080 --> 00:02:12,360
Thumb!

48
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:14,400
Minus five.

49
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:16,040
Push the upper bead up.

50
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:16,940
Thumb again!

51
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:18,340
Oh!

52
00:02:18,660 --> 00:02:20,100
Only three on the ones rod?

53
00:02:20,620 --> 00:02:21,780
Watch what happens next.

54
00:02:22,480 --> 00:02:24,820
Now carry one bead to the tens rod.

55
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:26,240
And there it is.

56
00:02:26,780 --> 00:02:28,600
Seven plus six is thirteen!

57
00:02:29,180 --> 00:02:31,240
That is our first family formula.

58
00:02:32,140 --> 00:02:33,620
Having fun with the family?

59
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:37,500
Give this video a like, and subscribe to meet the rest.

60
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:39,540
Bigger numbers now.

61
00:02:40,020 --> 00:02:41,060
Make twenty-six.

62
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:45,200
On the ones rod, one lower bead and the upper bead.

63
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:47,800
Then two lower beads on the tens rod.

64
00:02:48,340 --> 00:02:50,300
Thumb up, index finger down!

65
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:52,640
Seven's friend is three.

66
00:02:53,220 --> 00:02:55,040
Can we take away three lower beads?

67
00:02:56,920 --> 00:02:57,640
No!

68
00:02:58,240 --> 00:02:59,120
Only one.

69
00:02:59,760 --> 00:03:00,620
Stuck again.

70
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:01,920
Call the family.

71
00:03:02,480 --> 00:03:06,420
Plus seven equals plus two, minus five, plus ten.

72
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,080
Push two lower beads up.

73
00:03:11,060 --> 00:03:13,100
Now push the upper bead up.

74
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,280
Carry one bead to the tens rod.

75
00:03:16,760 --> 00:03:17,920
Thumb all the way!

76
00:03:18,460 --> 00:03:20,460
Twenty-six plus seven is thirty-three!

77
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:22,220
Look.

78
00:03:22,740 --> 00:03:26,980
Every time: plus some lower beads, minus five, plus ten.

79
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:28,960
Every move went up.

80
00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:31,020
So every move was a thumb.

81
00:03:31,700 --> 00:03:33,720
Plus six, add one.

82
00:03:34,160 --> 00:03:35,820
Plus seven, add two.

83
00:03:36,320 --> 00:03:38,000
Plus eight, add three.

84
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:40,200
Plus nine, add four.

85
00:03:40,660 --> 00:03:44,060
But minus five, and plus ten, never change.

86
00:03:45,460 --> 00:03:50,880
Four family formulas for adding: plus six, seven, eight and nine.

87
00:03:51,820 --> 00:03:52,740
Your turn.

88
00:03:53,180 --> 00:03:54,780
Make five on the ones rod.

89
00:03:55,140 --> 00:03:56,140
Just the upper bead.

90
00:03:56,560 --> 00:03:58,720
That is down, so use your index finger.

91
00:03:59,180 --> 00:04:00,320
Then add nine.

92
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:02,160
What is nine's friend?

93
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:04,120
One!

94
00:04:04,780 --> 00:04:05,820
Look at the ones rod.

95
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:07,940
There are no lower beads at all.

96
00:04:08,320 --> 00:04:09,200
So call the family.

97
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:11,940
Nine is how many more than five?

98
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:14,060
Four!

99
00:04:14,620 --> 00:04:18,420
Plus nine equals plus four, minus five, plus ten.

100
00:04:19,260 --> 00:04:20,760
Now do all three moves.

101
00:04:21,260 --> 00:04:24,260
Ones rod first, and remember, up is the thumb.

102
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:26,880
What number is showing now?

103
00:04:28,320 --> 00:04:30,360
Five plus nine is fourteen!

104
00:04:30,880 --> 00:04:31,740
Well done!

105
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:34,440
You did the family trick all by yourself.

106
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:38,020
So now you know the family trick for adding.

107
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:40,340
Try them at home on your own abacus.

108
00:04:40,820 --> 00:04:45,780
To meet the whole family, search for Abacus Kids on the Apple App Store or Google Play.

109
00:04:46,140 --> 00:04:46,980
Download it free.

110
00:04:47,580 --> 00:04:50,340
Next time, the family works the other way round.

111
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:52,980
We will learn the family trick for taking away.

112
00:04:53,440 --> 00:04:54,300
See you next time!
